## 3. Gradient System

Each theme defines 3 gradients. All gradients use a `135deg` angle.

### Gradient Definitions

| Gradient | Dark | Light | Vibrant | helloDarwin |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `--gradient-primary` | `hsl(195 100% 50%)` → `hsl(210 100% 60%)` | `hsl(270 91% 65%)` → `hsl(280 85% 55%)` | `hsl(330 100% 60%)` → `hsl(280 100% 65%)` | `hsl(300 60% 45%)` → `hsl(280 55% 50%)` |
| `--gradient-celebration` | `hsl(38 95% 55%)` → `hsl(45 100% 60%)` | `hsl(48 96% 53%)` → `hsl(45 100% 60%)` | `hsl(45 100% 55%)` → `hsl(30 100% 60%)` | `hsl(52 100% 50%)` → `hsl(45 100% 55%)` |
| `--gradient-success` | `hsl(142 76% 45%)` → `hsl(150 80% 50%)` | `hsl(160 84% 39%)` → `hsl(150 80% 45%)` | `hsl(150 100% 45%)` → `hsl(120 100% 50%)` | `hsl(168 76% 42%)` → `hsl(160 70% 45%)` |

### CSS Utility Classes

```css
.gradient-primary   { background: var(--gradient-primary); }
.gradient-celebration { background: var(--gradient-celebration); }
.gradient-success   { background: var(--gradient-success); }
```

### Usage Patterns

- `gradient-primary`: KPI card icons, logo square, celebration photo borders
- `gradient-celebration`: Fun Facts icon, accent highlights
- `gradient-success`: Success-themed KPI icons

